  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_da6b629d75284e799e46dffe995d0446",
      "statement": "GitHubService builds its outbound credential chain in its constructor: it reads the PEM at GitHub:PrivateKeyPath, imports it into an RSA instance, constructs an AppInstallationTokenProvider from AppId + that key + InstallationId + a GitHubAppTokenProvider, wraps it in an AppInstallationAuthProvider, and creates a Kiota HttpClientRequestAdapter via GitHub.Octokit.Client.RequestAdapter.Create before handing it to GitHubClient.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/GitHub/GitHubService.cs#L17-L21",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:edd82f0c2f6f0a00076b6409bbaba3d0aaa144e90c8a8a95bb0150aefa2fce63:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/GitHub/GitHubService.cs#L23-L38",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:918ac9ffdfb965cdb6c2cfc95cabe480f1e34a819d167361d3b1c3370247b38e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_9bb28cec73804221bf78bc04b0cc9516",
      "statement": "The credential settings have asymmetric validation: PrivateKeyPath is a path string (never key material) that is required, AppId is an int constrained to [Range(1, int.MaxValue)], and InstallationId is a plain required string that Sebastian never parses, so a malformed installation id survives startup and fails only when the SDK requests a token.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Configuration/SebastianConfig.cs#L20-L33",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:eb1a2544d5fac0e77f2ce4fd84de9b669df34c0ca580ab6c5c24df50624a3bba:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_8b2b089f1af74ba58f3fb872de7baf21",
      "statement": "GitHubService exposes exactly two write operations and no others: PostCommentAsync forwards the caller's string verbatim as the comment body to the issue comments endpoint, and CloseIssueAsync patches the issue with State = closed and StateReason = Not_planned, deliberately not completed.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/GitHub/GitHubService.cs#L40-L69",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0d35813228612814134624f4040cb51d61aac022ec123b62b02fe07731be9c3d:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_56ca3a5b37b34a57a487bd425b00ef1c",
      "statement": "The observable intake side effects are owned by the webhook processor, not the client: it composes the exact comment string 'Closed: the spec is missing required sections: <sections>.', calls PostCommentAsync before CloseIssueAsync so the reason survives closure, and has no try/catch around either call, so a failure propagates out of the webhook request and can leave one effect applied without the other.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Webhooks/GitHubWebhookProcessor.cs#L63-L82",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:61fd2ffce9308b6d2d577af4347ee4a46367ea92c77f5642f2a54f7bdf11d157:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d7cc0b35b00d4a1a8e8184de573b7746",
      "statement": "Program.cs resolves GitHubService eagerly right after Build() specifically so constructor-time credential failures abort startup, which converts an unreadable or invalid PEM into a deployment failure; because no network call is made during construction, a well-formed but mismatched AppId/InstallationId/key set instead fails on the first write during a webhook request.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Program.cs#L40-L44",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b36b1b1c86bb9d607d883845b284904cc9c67fc6b38a5dc26ebd25b756eb0b42:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/GitHub/GitHubService.cs#L27-L34",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:128870302ed000a7b442682c456dbe878f5cee0dc3060302747300c748f75f41:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c9de5f893b934188a44532d8a2ac202a",
      "statement": "GitHubService is registered as a root singleton implementing IDisposable, so one RSA key and one HTTP request adapter serve every request for the process lifetime (configuration and key rotation require a restart), and the host disposes it at shutdown in the order adapter first, then private key.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Program.cs#L19-L19",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:19cc96cae38f7f22b6eea8ad1addeed2ba13d6aa828744c6a5cd381e6ac60b0f:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/GitHub/GitHubService.cs#L71-L76",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:fbd5caed18584b11ee10fcff20b85b948339667dd83bc4fc4af6534039dd7d14:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_e7bc062abd834a27af8b69f363d7bc0f",
      "statement": "The write surface is deliberately thin and cannot be widened by configuration: no label write exists (both the feature and ready-for-agent labels are read-only filters), and no pull-request create/comment/review/merge operation exists, nor is ProcessPullRequestWebhookAsync overridden — so adding a label or PR operation means adding methods to GitHubService and extending the caller in GitHubWebhookProcessor.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/GitHub/GitHubService.cs#L40-L69",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0d35813228612814134624f4040cb51d61aac022ec123b62b02fe07731be9c3d:"
        },
        {
