          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a738bcc56ff2a6df6e42876fc9a2505ef09b6ec099f134d3c09da19ddd9c20bc:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Webhooks/GitHubWebhookProcessor.cs#L32-L49",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:64cd89c45f7399cfb2e43ec37f99f605b9bbae1ae09c44f78ab261cc8ea8e253:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_5689377ebf1944d697382922dc0a53c1",
      "statement": "The owner, repository, and issue number are supplied explicitly on every call from the webhook payload, so the client is scoped to the app installation rather than to the single repository the process mirrors; the owner/name cross-check against the parsed origin happens later in ImplementSpec.PrepareWorkspaceAsync, after intake has already been allowed to comment on and close the issue named by the delivery.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Agent/ImplementSpec.cs#L68-L76",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:712da247a86982f2c86bbdbd1202f86af79b9c18b336672ba4953a640a490545:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Webhooks/GitHubWebhookProcessor.cs#L51-L78",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0049575289d56ca14e86394888ad78269597a363b0eacbc2f7a1c075dcc18e5b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_52fde02d084b430f8f87a5ea6270051e",
      "statement": "Every SDK type in GitHubService is reached through global::-qualified aliases because the file's own namespace is Sebastian.GitHub, which shadows the GitHub root namespace; the aliases also name the generated nested payload types (CommentsPostRequestBody, WithIssue_numberPatchRequestBody) and disambiguate GitHubAppTokenProvider from AppInstallationTokenProvider.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/GitHub/GitHubService.cs#L1-L15",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bf24b415b0b3a0175b1f1fcad0875049a11a9bda44a6af62b1d6e8e68f877af8:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_426d6eb54acd4f55bad8431b3f805a51",
      "statement": "Outbound REST uses the Kiota-generated GitHub.Octokit.SDK plus Microsoft.Kiota.Bundle while inbound webhooks use Octokit.Webhooks.AspNetCore, so two separate GitHub SDKs coexist in the process; GitHubService contains no AOT accommodation (no DynamicDependency, JsonSerializerContext, or trimming roots), and the project's AOT settings and their justification are scoped to configuration binding.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Sebastian.csproj#L10-L24",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:51ef8bd52cf837f387813e84ff8a95b72f5fe8d457b333e89c5bd24f6b331343:"
